why Defensive Stance at 10 and a one-hand weapon of your choice: Uzzek's road, Brill's crypt, or the Skybreaker shield.

# The Horde Defensive Stance quests at level 10, every race in one guide:
# - Orc, Troll, Tauren (and Skyborne): Veteran Uzzek (1505) from the warrior
#   trainers of Razor Hill, Bloodhoof Village, Thunder Bluff or Orgrimmar,
#   Path of Defense (1498: Defensive Stance), then Thun'grim Firegaze and
#   Forged Steel (1502, 1503: a choice of Thun'grim's Axe, Mace, Dagger or
#   Sword).
# - Undead: Speak with Dillinger (1818) from Austil de Mon in Brill, Ulag the
#   Cleaver (1819: Defensive Stance), then Speak with Coleman, Agamand
#   Heirlooms and Heirloom Weapon (1820-1822: a choice of the Heirloom Axe,
#   Hammer, Dagger or Sword).
# - Skyborne: The Skybreaker Bulwark (94003, Forever-new) from Seena
#   Skybreaker in Valanaar on Zephras Isle (Defensive Stance and the
#   Stormforged Protector shield).
# The two Classic roads exclude each other (TDB exclusive groups: Veteran
# Uzzek with Speak with Dillinger, Path of Defense with Ulag the Cleaver);
# any Horde warrior may take either. The guide offers each race its home road
# first; the Brill steps carry no race filter, so an Orc, Troll, Tauren or
# Skyborne who takes Speak with Dillinger instead is led through it (Uzzek's
# steps pass once his quests are closed to them; the Brill steps carry
# `when !turnedin 1505`, so an Uzzek-road player never sees them). Lint warns
# that 1819 is closed after 1498 earlier in the chain: it reads
# the chain straight through and does not apply that `when`.
# Forever's quest data opens both to Skyborne-Horde; a Skyborne who already
# has the Bulwark's Defensive Stance can take Uzzek's road later for
# Thun'grim's weapon.
# Sources: quests.json, npcs.json, objects.json and items.json for the
# chains, givers, Ulag, the chest and the four Agamand Weapon Racks;
# quest-notes for the drop rates (Singed Scale 80%), levels, respawns, the
# skull plaque, the crypt's rooms and the chest's guards; Forever's Warrior
# class quest list (data/local/quest-audit/): Path of Defense and Ulag the
# Cleaver now teach Defensive Stance, Veteran Uzzek also starts at Torm
# Ragetotem, The Skybreaker Bulwark is new (Defensive Stance, Stormforged
# Protector). The leveling routes do these quests on the way (orc-troll
# 01-durotar and 03-the-barrens, tauren 01-mulgore, undead 01-tirisfal-glades,
# skyborne 01-zephras-isle); this guide is for anyone off the route.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Skyborne: The Skybreaker Bulwark

step Seena Skybreaker in Valanaar
  only Skyborne
  zone Zephras Isle
  tip At 10, Seena Skybreaker stands with the trainers by Valanaar's west gate. A cultist, Zaal Stormshield, holds her family's shield at the Shrine of Akir.
  level 10
  accept 94003                                -- Seena Skybreaker

step Zaal Stormshield
  only Skyborne
  tip Head north-west from Valanaar to the Shrine of Akir. Zaal Stormshield stands west of the shrine's approach, among the cult's Guardians, Spiritcallers and Blademasters: pull them one at a time before you take him. He drops the Skybreaker Bulwark.
  kill 257196                                 -- Zaal Stormshield
  collect 263993 quest 94003.1                -- Skybreaker Bulwark, from Zaal Stormshield

step The Skybreaker Bulwark
  only Skyborne
  tip Back to Seena in Valanaar. She teaches Defensive Stance and gives you the Stormforged Protector, a shield to use it with. Uzzek's road below still gives a weapon later, once you reach Kalimdor.
  turnin 94003 reward 275290                  -- Seena Skybreaker: Defensive Stance

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Orc, Troll, Tauren: Uzzek and Thun'grim

step Veteran Uzzek (Razor Hill)
  only Orc,Troll,Skyborne
  zone Durotar
  tip At 10, Tarshaw Jaggedscar, the warrior trainer in the barracks of Razor Hill, sends you to Uzzek in the Barrens. Sorek in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor offers it too. Any Horde warrior may take one of the two roads, never both: heading to Tirisfal Glades at 10 anyway? Austil de Mon in Brill's inn offers the other: one fight by Brill's graveyard for the same stance, then the Agamand crypt for an heirloom weapon.
  level 10
  accept 1505 npc 3169                        -- Tarshaw Jaggedscar

step Veteran Uzzek (Mulgore)
  only Tauren
  zone Mulgore
  tip At 10, Krang Stonehoof, the warrior trainer of Bloodhoof Village, sends you to Uzzek in the Barrens. Torm Ragetotem in Thunder Bluff offers it too.
  level 10
  accept 1505 npc 3063                        -- Krang Stonehoof

step Uzzek at Far Watch Post
  only Orc,Troll,Tauren,Skyborne
  zone The Barrens
  tip Uzzek is easy to miss: he stands under a small canopy by a large tree just west of Far Watch Post, below the road's south side, with the post in sight to his east. Going straight south from the post does not lead to him. From Durotar cross the bridge west; from Mulgore head north past the Crossroads.
  turnin 1505                                 -- Uzzek
  accept 1498

step Singed Scales in Thunder Ridge
  only Orc,Troll,Tauren,Skyborne
  zone Durotar
  tip You need five Singed Scales. Thunder Lizards (level 9-10) and Lightning Hides (10-11) live down in the Thunder Ridge crevasse in north-west Durotar, south of Orgrimmar: from the Barrens bridge turn left and follow the river north into it. Both drop a scale about four kills in five; both cast Lizard Bolt.
  collect 6486 x5 quest 1498.1                -- Singed Scale, from the lizards

step Path of Defense
  only Orc,Troll,Tauren,Skyborne
  zone The Barrens
  tip Back to Uzzek under his tree west of Far Watch Post.
  turnin 1498                                 -- Uzzek: Defensive Stance
  accept 1502

step Thun'grim Firegaze
  only Orc,Troll,Tauren,Skyborne
  tip Thun'grim's hut sits on top of Thorn Hill, east of the Crossroads. Most slopes are too steep: climb the broad ridge on the north or east side.
  turnin 1502                                 -- Thun'grim Firegaze
  accept 1503

step Forged Steel
  only Orc,Troll,Tauren,Skyborne
  tip The Stolen Iron Chest stands by a broken wagon in the Razormane camp north-west of Thun'grim, north-east of the Crossroads. Two Razormanes guard it and their hunters pull more quilboar: clear them one at a time, then open the chest (it refills within seconds, so a friend can loot it too).
  collect 6534 quest 1503.1                   -- Forged Steel Bars, from the Stolen Iron Chest
  turnin 1503 choose 7326 7328 7327 7329      -- Thun'grim Firegaze

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Brill (Undead, or anyone who took this road): Ulag and the Agamand heirlooms

step Speak with Dillinger
  only Undead
  zone Tirisfal Glades
  tip At 10, Austil de Mon, the warrior trainer inside the inn of Brill, sends you to Deathguard Dillinger by the graveyard on Brill's west edge. This road and Uzzek's exclude each other: drop Veteran Uzzek or Path of Defense from your log if you hold one.
  level 10
  accept 1818                                 -- Austil de Mon

step Deathguard Dillinger
  when !turnedin 1505
  zone Tirisfal Glades
  tip Dillinger stands by the graveyard on Brill's west edge. An Orc, Troll, Tauren or Skyborne who took Speak with Dillinger from Austil de Mon instead of Uzzek's road is led through Brill from here.
  turnin 1818                                 -- Deathguard Dillinger
  accept 1819

step Ulag the Cleaver
  when !turnedin 1505
  tip Ulag sleeps in the mausoleum in the graveyard just north of Dillinger. To wake him, click the flat skull plaque on the ground, left of the path to the mausoleum door; the seal lifts and Ulag (level 11, not elite) walks out. Start at full health.
  kill 6390 quest 1819.1                      -- Ulag the Cleaver
  turnin 1819                                 -- Deathguard Dillinger: Defensive Stance
  accept 1820

step Coleman Farthing
  when !turnedin 1505
  tip Coleman Farthing is in the Gallows' End Tavern, the inn on Brill's east side.
  turnin 1820                                 -- Coleman Farthing
  accept 1821

step The Agamand Family Crypt
  when !turnedin 1505
  tip The four Agamand Weapon Racks are inside the Agamand Family Crypt at the north end of Agamand Mills, north of Brill, one rack per room: one in the lowest room, two in the pair of rooms up the stairs, one in the room above those. The axe rack stands in a dark corner. The crypt's undead come in packs of three or more and return quickly; the ones in the top room are not linked. The axe, dagger and mace racks take 15 minutes to refill after someone loots them.
  collect 7567 quest 1821.1                   -- Agamand Family Axe
  collect 7568 quest 1821.2                   -- Agamand Family Dagger
  collect 7569 quest 1821.3                   -- Agamand Family Mace
  collect 7566 quest 1821.4                   -- Agamand Family Sword

step Back to Coleman Farthing
  when !turnedin 1505
  turnin 1821                                 -- Coleman Farthing
  accept 1822
  turnin 1822 choose 7115 7117 7116 7118      -- Coleman Farthing
